  "details": "1. Setup an Udon program to use `Networking.LocalPlayer.PlayHapticEventInHand` and provide it a negative amplitude.\n\n2. Build & Test or Publish the world for Android\n\n3. On an Android Flatscreen device launch the world.\n\n4. Activate the Udon program and notice the java illegal argument exception.\n\n`amplitude must either be DEFAULT_AMPLITUDE, or between 1 and 255 inclusive (amplitude=0)`\n\nTested with the parameters: `Right`, `0.1`, `0`, `1`. Notably this does not cause an exception on Meta Quest native (Quest 2 on open-beta).\n\nThis includes the value 0 as well as negative values which has been noted to be an issue in this world: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_937e9703-1aff-4963-b3aa-84375c47796f",
